  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 1204 PM MST Thu Nov 19 2026\n\nSaturday...Shortwave trough energy moves past the forecast area, \nwith most locations remaining dry. 700 mb temperatures near -7 \nCelsius will yield high temperatures in the lower 30s to lower 40s.\n\nSunday...Dry west southwest flow aloft prevails. The atmosphere \nlooks too dry at low and mid levels for any precipitation. \n\nMonday...The flow aloft backs to southwest in advance of the next \nshortwave trough aloft approaching from Utah. Scattered coverage of \norographic snows on tap for our Snowy and Sierra Madre Ranges. 700 \nmb temperatures near -5 Celsius will yield high temperatures in the \n30s.\n\nTuesday...The next open trough aloft moves over the forecast area, \nwith a chance of rain and snow early in the day, then drying noted \nin the afternoon. \n\nWednesday...Shortwave ridging develops across Wyoming, keeping it \ndry. A warming trend develops with downslope warming and rising 700 \nmb temperatures.\n\nThursday...Another shortwave trough aloft moves across Wyoming with \nscattered coverage of orographic snow showers for our Snowy and \nSierra Madre Ranges, dry elsewhere. Similar temperatures when \ncompared to Wednesday with 700 mb temperatures nearly the same.",
